lesson: 205
title: Legs on a mixed farm
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: On a farm, cows, pigs, sheep and goats walk on 4 legs, while chickens and ducks stand on 2.
explain: Count the four-legged animals together, then the two-legged ones, and add the two counts of legs.
explain: 3 cows, 4 pigs and 10 chickens: (3 + 4) × 4 + 10 × 2 = 28 + 20 = 48 legs.
vars: a=name b=name c=2..9 p=2..9 h=2..15
answer: 4 * (c + p) + 2 * h
exercise: A farm has {c} cows, {p} pigs and {h} chickens. How many legs do the animals have?
exercise: {a} visits a farm with {c} sheep, {p} goats and {h} ducks. How many legs are there in all?
exercise: In the farmyard there are {h} chickens, {c} pigs and {p} goats. How many legs do they have altogether?
exercise: How many legs do {c} cows, {p} sheep and {h} ducks have together?
exercise: {a}'s uncle keeps {p} goats, {c} cows and {h} chickens. How many legs do his animals have?
exercise: {c} cows {p} pigs {h} chickens on the farm visit. legs?
exercise: farm had {c} sheep, {p} goats and like {h} ducks, smelt awful lol. how many legs
exercise: {h} chickens, sorry {h} hens, plus {c} cows and {p} pigs. legs total
exercise: we saw {c} pigs, {p} cows — no wait {p} sheep — and {h} ducks. how many legs
exercise: {b} reckons chickens got 4 legs. nope. {c} cows, {p} goats, {h} chickens, how many legs then
exercise: on the farm: {c} cows and {p} pigs, {h} chickens running round, and the farmer's tractor was broken. legs on the animals?
test: Find the number of legs on {h} ducks, {p} goats and {c} cows.
test: {b} counts the animals at a petting farm: {h} chickens in the run, and {c} sheep and {p} pigs in the field. How many legs are there?
test: What is the total number of legs on a farm with {p} pigs, {h} ducks and {c} goats?
test: There are {c} cows in the barn and {p} sheep beside it, while {h} hens peck in the yard. Count all the legs.
test: legs on {c} cows + {p} pigs + {h} chickens?
test: {h} ducks n {c} goats n {p} pigs at the farm, how many legs all up
exam: Determine the aggregate number of legs possessed by {c.words} cows, {p.words} pigs and {h.words} chickens kept upon a farm.
exam: It is given that an agricultural holding maintains {c} sheep, {p} goats and {h} ducks. Ascertain the total quantity of legs pertaining to the livestock.
exam: A census of a farmyard enumerates {h} hens, {c} cows and {p} pigs. Compute the number of legs belonging to all animals so enumerated.
exam: Whereas {p} goats and {c} cows graze in one field and {h} ducks occupy the adjoining pond, state the combined number of legs of these animals.
exercise: Grandad's farm had {c+1} cows, {p} pigs and {h} hens, but the oldest cow was sent to the knacker's yard. How many legs are on the farm now?
exercise: {a} said the farm has {c+2} sheep, but {a.he} was stretching the truth: it has {c} sheep, {p} goats and {h} ducks. How many legs are there in all?
test: fox 'paid a visit' to the hens, {h} left. plus {c} cows n {p} pigs. legs total, quick before the bloody farmer comes
